WEBVTT

00:00:03.188 --> 00:00:05.035
Choose the Telnyx tab.

00:00:05.035 --> 00:00:07.672
A blue panel lists the four steps.

00:00:07.672 --> 00:00:12.618
Before you start, create an API key, version 2, in the Telnyx portal.

00:00:12.618 --> 00:00:16.904
Sign in as an account owner or admin, so the key can create

00:00:16.904 --> 00:00:18.618
what the site needs.

00:00:19.074 --> 00:00:24.492
Tick Enable Telnyx provider, paste the key into API key, and click Save.

00:00:24.492 --> 00:00:26.854
The key is stored encrypted.

00:00:27.613 --> 00:00:31.419
Once the key is stored, a Connect Telnyx button appears.

00:00:31.419 --> 00:00:36.884
Clicking it creates the call application, the connection and the voice profile that

00:00:36.884 --> 00:00:40.813
Telnyx needs, and shows a green Connected to Telnyx panel.

00:00:42.413 --> 00:00:47.153
After you connect, the page also asks for the Default outbound caller id,

00:00:47.153 --> 00:00:52.073
the number your customers see, and the Webhook public key, which proves that

00:00:52.073 --> 00:00:54.593
call events really come from Telnyx.

00:00:54.593 --> 00:00:57.293
Without that key, calls do not connect.

00:00:58.043 --> 00:01:03.035
It also offers Noise suppression, which cleans background sound out of calls, and

00:01:03.035 --> 00:01:06.592
an Advanced section for rarely changed network settings.

00:01:06.592 --> 00:01:08.773
Every one has a working default.

